     "t": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "import random\n\ndef reservoir(stream, k, seed=0):\n    rnd = random.Random(seed)\n    sample = []\n    for i, item in enumerate(stream):\n        if i < k:\n            sample.append(item)\n        else:\n            j = rnd.randint(0, i)          # replace with probability k/(i+1)\n            if j < k:\n                sample[j] = item\n    return sample\n\nprint(reservoir(range(1000), 5))          # Output: [819, 785, 2, 930, 506]\nprint(len(reservoir(range(10), 3)))       # Output: 3\nprint(sorted(reservoir(range(3), 5)))     # Output: [0, 1, 2]\n\n# One pass, O(k) memory, and you never need to know the stream's length.",
